  "id": "COMPOUND:383 - PROTEIN:899",
  "verbalization": "Carisoprodol is implicated in the targeting of Gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) receptor subunit alpha-5 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that carisoprodol acts as a target for GABA receptor subunit alpha-1, which in turn is targeted by ganaxolone and zopiclone, both of which are known to interact with GABA receptors. This indicates a potential mechanism where carisoprodol may influence the GABA receptor subunit alpha-5 through its interaction with these related compounds. The consistent targeting of alpha-5 across different compounds suggests a broader role for GABA receptor subunit alpha-5 in the pharmacological effects of these drugs. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of GABA receptor subunit alpha-5 in the action of carisoprodol and its related compounds, reinforcing the notion of a shared mechanism in their pharmacological profile.",
